{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789661309,"nonce":"4BjWDfkanBj+x8fEea4/ujVccXE=","title":"Typed relations with inverses and cardinality; parent is a relation","message":"`AddRelation{type, target entity.Id}` / `RemoveRelation`. Relation types come from the schema with inverse and cardinality: `parent`/`child` (parent cardinality 1), `blocks`/`blocked-by`, `relates`, `duplicates`. Hierarchy = type list + allowed-parent rules + the parent relation, so Linear (Initiative \u003e Project \u003e Issue \u003e sub-issue) and Jira (Initiative \u003e Epic \u003e Story/Task \u003e Subtask) are both config.\n\nPer AGENTS.md: cross-issue links are ops storing the other id, resolved via entity.Resolvers, eventually consistent; the inverse is *derived* at read time, not written to the other entity (no multi-entity commit). Dangling targets must render, not crash.","files":null},{"type":9,"timestamp":1789661309,"nonce":"kk5931dJ1H9L7dwaAVe26J0LI+A=","key":"type","value":"task"},{"type":9,"timestamp":1789661309,"nonce":"tr9ru6hkr0ADLxbhiLA1YbDS21g=","key":"status","value":"to-do"}]}